# suite TSOEXPEV export evidence and V
ok 1 - an unknown function is refused, not obeyed
ok 2 - a despatch reference is required
ok 3 - a domestic VAT code is refused on an export
ok 4 - the United States is rest of world
ok 5 - no commodity code blocks the customs hand-off
ok 6 - the blocked line is named
ok 7 - the proof deadline is three months from supply
ok 8 - the evidence is pending until proof arrives
ok 9 - the default permitted period is three months
ok 10 - three months with no proof becomes OVERDUE
ok 11 - the VAT that falls due is reported
ok 12 - an exception is raised for the VAT owner
ok 13 - the despatch is left marked OVERDUE
ok 14 - a GB to NI movement is a UK domestic supply
ok 15 - a GB to NI movement is not an export
ok 16 - a UK domestic supply needs no proof of export
ok 17 - proof of export needs both a type and a date
ok 18 - proof obtained after the permitted period fails
ok 19 - late proof is reported as EXP0008
ok 20 - late proof leaves the VAT due at 20 per cent
ok 21 - proof inside the period evidences the zero rate
ok 22 - evidenced export carries no VAT
ok 23 - an evidenced export is no longer overdue
ok 24 - the proof is written to the despatch itself
1..24
# TSOEXPEV export evidence and V passed 00024 failed 00000
# exit 0
